worker as a constructor (unused)"] [327 1 "// encodeModule is the image of a module's forms."] [341 2 "// a loader of its own: names and constructors are records, nothing is loaded or run"] [438 2 "// the file: header, string table, module, code"] [453 1 "// closure writes a top-level closure's compiled code, or the error compiling it gives (raised when entered)."] [490 1 "// ---- the reader ----"] [700 1 "// imgSpan is a top-level closure's code in its module's image."] [703 1 "// loadImage loads a module from its image (as loadForms from its forms)."] [734 2 "// phase 0: the binders (strings, then bindings: their order in the image)"] [747 2 "// the bindings, read once: closures made at once, constructors' atoms after every binder is known"] [784 2 "// phase 1: the objects"] [811 2 "// phase 2: the constructors' fields"] [822 1 "// atom0 skips an atom (its literal's string literal not made)."] [839 1 "// reg registers a top-level binder of the module."] [849 1 "// compileImage decodes a top-level closure's code from its module's image."] [864 1 "// imgStrs is the image's string table (read again: the module keeps only the bytes)."] [879 1 "// imagePath is a module's image under the image directory, or \"\" when there is none or it is stale."] [888 1 "// SetImageDir makes the machine load the libraries' modules from their images in dir when they are fresh."] [891 1 "// Images is the number of modules loaded from their images."] [894 1 "// BuildImages writes the image of every module of the units in libs (as the loader finds them) that has no fresh"] [895 1 "// one under out, jobs at a time: the images made, those already fresh, the errors."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[52 49] [56 39] [74 32] [236 27] [330 20] [391 24] [459 21] [610 16] [655 16] [664 16] [717 17] [717 25] [720 18] [720 26] [741 17] [741 25] [779 14] [779 23] [928 12] [928 22]]} (go/file "image.go" :imports [


